DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("e^((ln(x)))");
$fun_1 = Formula("(1*x)^2+5*((x)^(1/3))+5");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_3 = Compute("((8, infinity) - (((((8, infinity)))) U (8, infinity)))");
$set_ans_4 = Compute("((8, infinity) - ((-infinity, infinity) - (8, infinity))) U {-3, 0, 4, 5, 7} U ((8, infinity)) - ((-infinity, infinity) - ({-3, 0, 4, 5, 7} U {-2, 10}))");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("[4, 8] - ((-infinity, infinity) - [9, infinity)) U (([4, 8] U [9, infinity)) - ((-infinity, infinity) - ({-10, -7}))) U ((([4, 8])) U {-10, -7})");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("([4, 8] - [9, infinity))");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

- _For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._
- _For derivative problems, if the result is undefined, then *leave the blank empty*._

What is the value of [`15+10-2+13*6`]? [_____]{answer=>Real(101.),width=>1}
---

[`14+8-19*3`] is equal to [_____]{answer=>-35,width=>3}
---

What is the value of [`9+10+1-3`]? [_____]{answer=>Formula('17'),width=>4}
---

[`16+13-16-15`] is equal to [_____]{answer=>-2,width=>3}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | x \geq 9\}`]
- [`B = \{x | 4 \leq x \leq 8\}`]
- [`C = \{-10, -7\}`]

Compute:
- [`B \cap A \cup ((B \cup A) \cap (C)) \cup (((B)) \cup C) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`B - A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-2, 10\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x > 7\}`]
- [`C = \{-3, 0, 4, 5, 7\}`]

Compute:
- [`B - ((((B))) \cup B) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}
- [`(B \cap B) \cup C \cup (B) \cap (C \cup A) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -5, -10, -5 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -3, -5, 2 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-3, -5, 2>"))}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-3, -5, 2>") x Compute("<-5, -10, -5>")}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-3, -5, 2>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-5, -10, -5>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-5, -10, -5>"))}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -8, -7, 2 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -7, -9, 9 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 2, 8, 5 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-8, -7, 2>") . Compute("<2, 8, 5>")}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-7, -9, 9>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<2, 8, 5>"))}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-8, -7, 2>"))}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}
- [`f'(5) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>5)}
- [`f'(2) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>2)}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
